1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,460
Quentin Tarantino, one of the most acclaimed filmmakers of all time,

2
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:08,160
known for bringing his bold ideas to life with surreal visuals and mind-bending storytelling.

3
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:10,460
But he wasn't always a Hollywood icon.

4
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:13,780
Once he was just an ordinary guy working at a video store.

5
00:00:14,260 --> 00:00:16,940
Until one night, he decided to rewrite his story.

6
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:18,560
And there was like one night.

7
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:21,680
Stay up all night long, and rather than give myself excuses,

8
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:27,060
I would look at everything that I'm up in my life, or everything I'm not doing, or whatever,

9
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:29,640
and just not give myself any excuses out.

10
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:31,620
Just like nail it.

11
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:35,560
And I would spend like all night laying out everything I'm doing that's wrong.

12
00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:38,640
And then I would spend the last two hours figuring out how I can change it.

13
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:42,480
And as opposed to just doing it and then going to get some sleep.

14
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:43,700
I decided to change my life.

15
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:46,040
Today I present you the Tarantino Method.

16
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:48,560
To follow this process, you'll need three things.

17
00:00:48,740 --> 00:00:50,980
A pen, a notepad, and the dead of night.

18
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:53,540
When the world is silent and not a soul is awake.

19
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:55,000
That's when it can happen.

20
00:00:55,440 --> 00:00:55,760
Trust.

21
00:00:55,980 --> 00:00:56,840
Now it begins.

22
00:00:56,840 --> 00:00:58,920
The first page is always going to be the hardest.

23
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:03,080
I'm honest, but it's really all about getting that ball rolling.

24
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:08,680
Now that you've started, you have to ask yourself the big, scary, fear-mongering question.

25
00:01:08,680 --> 00:01:20,007
What am I doing wrong Be brutally honest As Quinton himself would say nail it Take your time Dive deep It gritty It tough But it absolutely necessary

26
00:01:20,747 --> 00:01:24,127
And when you push through, boom, you're halfway there.

27
00:01:26,467 --> 00:01:31,767
It's all out there. The fears, the doubts, the mistakes, the lessons, the heartbreak,

28
00:01:31,767 --> 00:01:37,607
all laid out, bare for you to see. Not built up in your mind, but on paper. Tangible.

29
00:01:38,927 --> 00:01:43,827
Take a moment, because now you have to ask yourself, how can I change it?

30
00:01:44,267 --> 00:01:45,967
We're not all Quentin Tarantino.

31
00:01:46,307 --> 00:01:48,327
You might be feeling like you're all written out.

32
00:01:48,727 --> 00:01:50,207
So let's make this part simple.

33
00:01:50,607 --> 00:01:51,787
A straightforward list.

34
00:01:52,267 --> 00:01:54,187
A hundred ways you can change your life.

35
00:01:54,407 --> 00:01:55,387
Quite a simple process.

36
00:01:56,107 --> 00:01:59,107
Take a mistake you've learned, and write down a way to change it.

37
00:01:59,727 --> 00:02:00,327
Repeat it.

38
00:02:00,507 --> 00:02:02,047
Over and over again.

39
00:02:02,187 --> 00:02:02,967
Push forward.

40
00:02:03,167 --> 00:02:03,767
Write it down.

41
00:02:04,027 --> 00:02:04,507
Adapt.

42
00:02:04,827 --> 00:02:05,267
Reflect.

43
00:02:05,267 --> 00:02:05,767
Learn.

44
00:02:06,207 --> 00:02:06,627
And grow.

45
00:02:06,627 --> 00:02:10,367
Until finally, when you ask yourself, how can I change my life?

46
00:02:10,487 --> 00:02:11,827
You'll have a hundred ways to do it.

47
00:02:11,967 --> 00:02:15,367
But there's one very important thing you need to remember throughout this whole night.

48
00:02:15,567 --> 00:02:17,147
You gotta actually f***ing do it.
